    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "01. Core Concepts",
    "ruleNumber": "01.02",
    "summary": "A unit acts together. Its opening model count sets Starting Strength, including attached models. Compare remaining wounds to W for a unit that started with one model. Otherwise compare the number of survivors with the opening count. Exactly half qualifies as Half-Strength. Splitting before battle resets each resulting unit’s count. A qualifying model can satisfy a unit descriptor. An effect that gives the unit a rule applies across its models. When replacing a model, align the new model’s centre to the original marked point, using the central axis for FRAME. If another model or the board edge prevents this, place it as near the point as possible.",
